nodecode-plan-mode is a rewrite of 100yenadmin's 100yenadmin/hermes-plan-mode:

  https://github.com/100yenadmin/hermes-plan-mode
  commit ee4a245fbc2b2d874f3a5021963bef6c358d17fb (2026-10-17)
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 100yenadmin (LICENSE)

The plugin is unchanged in what it gives a user: an enforced plan mode in
which the agent explores with read-only work, writes a plan file, shows it,
and changes nothing else until the operator approves it, after which it
implements the plan in the same turn. Rewritten in Common Lisp against
Nodecode's cell contract, so all of it is new code: one :TOOL hook that
reads an EVAL call's form and refuses the ones that write or run something
(the Hermes plugin's pre_tool_call allowlist, over the tools this organism
actually has), one plan_mode tool, one /plan command, and the standing
prompt note as a harness section instead of an injected turn note. The plan
is still a Markdown file under the working directory's plan folder, and
approval is still the operator's own act.

Left out, and why: Hermes's four approval surfaces (native buttons, a
clarify card, the classic panel, reactions) become Nodecode's one question
card plus the typed /plan approve, because Nodecode has one question board;
"approve and review each file edit" is not offered, since Nodecode's edits
are EVAL forms rather than a write_file/patch pair to interrupt; todo_list
progress mirroring, the per-channel footers, the profile and lever switches
(plan_once, codex_compact, skill policy) and the bug-report skill are
Hermes surfaces or taste knobs rather than the mode; the plans live under
.nodecode/plans instead of .hermes/plans.
